  "headline": "FSSAI Initiates Legal Action Against Bisleri Over Bacterial Presence",
  "seoTitle": "FSSAI Prosecutes Bisleri Over Unsafe Water",
  "metaDescription": "The FSSAI has launched legal proceedings against Bisleri International after lab tests identified coliform bacteria in samples from West Bengal and Goa.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) has started legal proceedings against Bisleri International regarding water safety.",
    "Laboratory tests confirmed the presence of coliform bacteria in water samples collected from production facilities in West Bengal and Goa.",
    "Bisleri maintains its products are safe for consumption and is coordinating with the regulator while specific batches are being withdrawn."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) is currently conducting a nationwide enforcement campaign focused on the quality of packaged drinking water. This broader initiative follows the detection of irregularities in specific samples processed by Bisleri International. In response to findings of coliform bacteria in samples originating from plants in West Bengal and Goa, the regulatory body has moved to initiate formal prosecution. While the FSSAI has ordered the restriction of sales for the identified batches, Bisleri International has publicly contested the safety concerns, asserting that its products meet quality standards and highlighting that it is actively cooperating with authorities to resolve the matter. The ongoing regulatory scrutiny has prompted an expansion of quality checks across the wider bottled water industry, with officials noting that comprehensive test results for the national surveillance drive are expected to be finalized within the next two months.",
